🔍 Parameter-by-Parameter Explanation
Parameter	Type	Purpose / Usage
cacheName	String	Unique name for the cache. Used as a key in the registry map and passed to the cacheManager.
keyType	Class<K>	Specifies the Java type of the cache key (e.g. String.class, Long.class). Ensures type safety.
valueType	Class<V>	Specifies the Java type of the cache value (e.g. User.class, Product.class).
ttlSeconds	long	Time-To-Live: how long an entry should stay in cache before it expires. Measured in seconds.
heapEntries	long	Max number of entries in the heap (JVM memory). Eviction (usually LRU) starts after this limit.
offheapMB	long	Max size (in MB) for storing entries in off-heap (native) memory, which avoids JVM GC pressure.
diskMB	long	Max size (in MB) to store entries on disk. Used only if properties.isDiskEnabled() is true.




Cache<String, User> userCache = dynamicCacheService.getOrCreateCache(
    "userCache",
    String.class,
    User.class,
    600,     // TTL 600 seconds
    1000,    // Heap entries
    50,      // Offheap MB
    200      // Disk MB (used only if disk is enabled)
);




| Concept      | Value Source  | Use In Code                         |
| ------------ | ------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Cache Name   | `cacheName`   | `registry`, `cacheManager`          |
| Key Type     | `keyType`     | `CacheConfigurationBuilder.new...`  |
| Value Type   | `valueType`   | Same                                |
| TTL          | `ttlSeconds`  | `ExpiryPolicyBuilder.timeToLive...` |
| Heap Tier    | `heapEntries` | `.heap(..., EntryUnit.ENTRIES)`     |
| Offheap Tier | `offheapMB`   | `.offheap(..., MemoryUnit.MB)`      |
| Disk Tier    | `diskMB`      | `.disk(..., MemoryUnit.MB, true)`   |



| Parameter                | Type         | Used In                                              | Purpose                                                                                       |
| ------------------------ | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `heapEntries`            | `long`       | `.heap(heapEntries, EntryUnit.ENTRIES)`              | Maximum number of entries to store in the **Java heap** (in-JVM memory). Fastest access.      |
| `EntryUnit.ENTRIES`      | `EntryUnit`  | Same as above                                        | Tells Ehcache that `heapEntries` is a **count of objects**, not memory size.                  |
| `offheapMB`              | `long`       | `.offheap(offheapMB, MemoryUnit.MB)`                 | Amount of **off-heap memory** (outside JVM) to allocate in **megabytes**. Avoids GC pressure. |
| `MemoryUnit.MB`          | `MemoryUnit` | Used to specify the **unit of size** (MB, GB, etc.). |                                                                                               |
| `diskMB`                 | `long`       | `.disk(diskMB, MemoryUnit.MB, true)`                 | Amount of **disk space** in MB to allocate for overflow or persistence.                       |
| `true` (in `.disk(...)`) | `boolean`    | Persistent flag                                      | `true` = persist data to disk **across JVM restarts**. `false` = temporary disk cache.        |
